[28.7675, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[16A\r\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mThe edit tool determined that the old and new were identical \u2014 probably I typed the same characters in both. \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mLet me carefully rewrite just that line: the correct characters are \u964d\u51aa (ji\u00e0ng m\u00ec, \"descend to a power\"?    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mno, that's not it). In Chinese: \"\u964d\u51aa\" means descending order, \"\u5347\u51aa\" means ascending order. Characters: \u964d  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128m(ji\u00e0ng), \u51aa (m\u00ec, power). Wait, is \"\u51aa\" the correct simplified form of \"\u51aa\"? The simplified form is \u5e42, and   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mthe traditional form is \u51aa. Hmm: \"\u5e42\" is the simplified form of \u51aa (power). In traditional Chinese: \u51aa? Let  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mme think. The character \u51aa (m\u00ec) means \"power\" \u2014 simplified as \u5e42. In fact, \"\u51aa\" (U+519A) is the              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mvariant/traditional form of \u51aa (U+515C). Common traditional usage: \u51aa. In simplified: \u5e42.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K                                                                                                              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mSo in traditional: \u964d\u51aa, \u5347\u51aa. What I wrote was \"\u964d\u51aa\", which contains \u51aa U+519A? I need to check what's     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mactually in the file. The edit failed because old and new were identical \u2014 I ended up pasting the same       \u001b[0m\u0